ers with at least 3 character classes, verified enforcement (rejects short/low-diversity passwords, accepts compliant ones) both before and after a full node restart, then cleaned up test users.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected /etc/security/pwquality.conf and PAM system-auth/password-auth wiring on node1 (RHEL 7.9, pam_pwquality already active via requisite)\",\"Appended 'minlen = 12' and 'minclass = 3' to /etc/security/pwquality.conf via sudo\",\"Created test user pwtestuser and verified via real PAM password-change flow (su + passwd) that: <11-char password rejected, 12+ char password with only 2 classes rejected, 12+ char password with 3 classes accepted\",\"Deleted pwtestuser\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime -s, pwquality.conf content, PAM config\",\"Issued backgrounded 'shutdown -r now' on node1 so the ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again; confirmed new boot_id and fresh uptime -s, proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Re-verified pwquality.conf and PAM config persisted post-restart\",\"Re-ran full live enforcement test post-restart with a second test user (pwtestuser2): weak/2-class password rejected, compliant 3-class 13-char password accepted\",\"Deleted pwtestuser2 and confirmed both test users no longer exist\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"minlen=12 and minclass=3 configured on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-514e4170c0fb4b3e\",\"cmd-db3257c36231425b\"],\"summary\":\"pwquality.conf shows minlen=12 and minclass=3 both immediately after edit and again after the node restart, proving the setting is in place and persistent.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Policy actually enforced for new user passwords (length + character classes)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d225d74e79de4fbc\",\"cmd-9e6abdc9a9f84f08\",\"cmd-77778be8e3664ccb\",\"cmd-1897a4109e7c4bbe\",\"cmd-b5c992dec1054294\"],\"summary\":\"Live passwd attempts via PAM as a non-root user show short passwords and passwords with fewer than 3 character classes are rejected with pwquality errors, while a 12+ character password with 3 classes is accepted (exit 0).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5e3ffe3552764ede\"],\"summary\":\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (d7a80301-...), uptime -s, and confirmed pwquality.conf/PAM config were correctly in place before disrupting the node.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d7692a8384a943ca\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'shutdown -r now' returned REBOOT_ACK immediately, before the node went unreachable.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node actually restarted (changed boot identity)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-027f55fa912046ab\",\"cmd-6a0877df9bc4464b\"],\"summary\":\"First poll after reboot command failed with connection timeout (node down); subsequent poll succeeded with a new boot_id (6930b99c-...) and fresh uptime -s (2026-09-04 23:34:32), differing from the pre-restart boot_id, proving a real restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required config and live enforcement\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-db3257c36231425b\",\"cmd-92313573caa540a1\",\"cmd-e0ddf1015ef54eef\"],\"summary\":\"After restart, pwquality.conf and PAM wiring were intact, and a fresh live PAM password-change test again rejected a non-compliant password and accepted a compliant one; test users were then removed, confirmed via failed 'id' lookups.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to require new user passwords be at least 12 characters with at least 3 character classes, verified enforcement (rejects short/low-diversity passwords, accepts compliant ones) both before and after a full node restart, then cleaned up test users.","actions_performed":["Inspected /etc/security/pwquality.conf and PAM system-auth/password-auth wiring on node1 (RHEL 7.9, pam_pwquality already active via requisite)","Appended 'minlen = 12' and 'minclass = 3' to /etc/security/pwquality.conf via sudo","Created test user pwtestuser and verified via real PAM password-change flow (su + passwd) that: <11-char password rejected, 12+ char password with only 2 classes rejected, 12+ char password with 3 classes accepted","Deleted pwtestuser","Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime -s, pwquality.conf content, PAM config","Issued backgrounded 'shutdown -r now' on node1 so the ack returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again; confirmed new boot_id and fresh uptime -s, proving an actual restart occurred","Re-verified pwquality.conf and PAM config persisted post-restart","Re-ran full live enforcement test post-restart with a second test user (pwtestuser2): weak/2-class password rejected, compliant 3-class 13-char password accepted","Deleted pwtestuser2 and confirmed both test users no longer exist"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"minlen=12 and minclass=3 configured on node1","command_ids":["cmd-514e4170c0fb4b3e","cmd-db3257c36231425b"],"summary":"pwquality.conf shows minlen=12 and minclass=3 both immediately after edit and again after the node restart, proving the setting is in place and persistent."},{"requirement":"Policy actually enforced for new user passwords (length + character classes)","command_ids":["cmd-d225d74e79de4fbc","cmd-9e6abdc9a9f84f08","cmd-77778be8e3664ccb","cmd-1897a4109e7c4bbe","cmd-b5c992dec1054294"],"summary":"Live passwd attempts via PAM as a non-root user show short passwords and passwords with fewer than 3 character classes are rejected with pwquality errors, while a 12+ character password with 3 classes is accepted (exit 0)."},{"requirement":"Healthy baseline captured before restart","command_ids":["cmd-5e3ffe3552764ede"],"summary":"Captured pre-restart boot_id (d7a80301-...), uptime -s, and confirmed pwquality.conf/PAM config were correctly in place before disrupting the node."},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-d7692a8384a943ca"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'shutdown -r now' returned REBOOT_ACK immediately, before the node went unreachable."},{"requirement":"Node actually restarted (changed boot identity)","command_ids":["cmd-027f55fa912046ab","cmd-6a0877df9bc4464b"],"summary":"First poll after reboot command failed with connection timeout (node down); subsequent poll succeeded with a new boot_id (6930b99c-...) and fresh uptime -s (2026-09-04 23:34:32), differing from the pre-restart boot_id, proving a real restart."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of required config and live enforcement","command_ids":["cmd-db3257c36231425b","cmd-92313573caa540a1","cmd-e0ddf1015ef54eef"],"summary":"After restart, pwquality.conf and PAM wiring were intact, and a fresh live PAM password-change test again rejected a non-compliant password and accepted a compliant one; test users were then removed, confirmed via failed 'id' lookups."}]},"ttft_ms":3316,"type":"result","duration_ms":110924,"uuid":"2a89f51f-9a4d-4997-878e-a7d7f80fb3ec","ttft_stream_ms":1518,"time_to_request_ms":43,"first_content_frame_ms":2115,"queued_turn_count":0}
